    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The selected passage permits overseas contributions to count towards the minimum period but
      distinguishes their treatment in the amount calculation.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol12-ch74/0014
      quote: "74154 Contributions paid by a person who has worked or resided outside the UK may count towards the\n\
        minimum period of 10 qualifying years."
      locator: DMG 74154
    - page: page/dmg-vol12-ch74/0014
      quote: "74162 Although contributions paid by a person who has worked or resided outside the UK may count\n\
        towards the minimum period of 10 qualifying years, they are not included when deciding the amount of\nSP.
        Therefore, a person may receive less than 10/35 of the full rate of SP."
      locator: DMG 74162
